From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Refael Ackermann <refack@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:37:43 -0400
Subject: Carry the TortoiseGit repository-switch hooks forward to 2.55

These three functions exist only for gitdll, which re-points a long-lived
process at a different repository. Upstream git sets up one repository and
exits, so 2.55 restructuring moved the ground under all of them at once.

odb_close_tgit(): odb_source became polymorphic and only the files backend
owns packs, so source->packfiles is gone. Downcast with
odb_source_files_downcast(), guarded on type == ODB_SOURCE_FILES because that
helper BUG()s on anything else and alternates need not be files-backed. What
this adds over upstream odb_close() is unchanged: closing the handles is not
enough, the store also has to forget which packs it found, because TGitCache
and gitdll outlive any single repack.

reset_setup(): the four file-scope caches it cleared no longer exist.
setup state lives in struct repository now, and is_inside_git_dir() and
is_inside_work_tree() recompute per call rather than memoising. The one that
did survive, git_work_tree_initialized, became repo->worktree_initialized and
is handled where it belongs, in repo_clear(). Kept as an empty marker rather
than deleted, because it names a requirement upstream has no reason to
preserve and setup.c may well cache again.

reset_git_env(): test the_repository->initialized rather than ->objects
before clearing. initialize_repository() sets the flag but not the object
database, which only appears later during setup_git_directory(), so a
git_init() that never opened an odb used to skip the clear and then trip
2.55 new "repository initialized already" BUG().
---
 environment.c |  9 ++++++++-
 odb.c         | 21 ++++++++++++++++++---
 setup.c       | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 3 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/environment.c b/environment.c
index 38207e1160..e247e20085 100644
--- a/environment.c
+++ b/environment.c
@@ -733,7 +733,14 @@ void reset_git_env(const LPCWSTR *env)
 	FREE_AND_NULL(comment_line_str_to_free);
 	auto_comment_line_char = 0;
 	is_bare_repository_cfg = -1;
-	if (the_repository && the_repository->objects)
+	/*
+	 * Test ->initialized, not ->objects: initialize_repository() sets the
+	 * flag but not the object database, which only appears later during
+	 * setup_git_directory(). A git_init() that never got as far as opening
+	 * an odb would otherwise skip the clear and then BUG() here on the
+	 * "repository initialized already" guard v2.55 added.
+	 */
+	if (the_repository && the_repository->initialized)
 		repo_clear(the_repository);
 	initialize_repository(the_repository);
 	FREE_AND_NULL(git_work_tree_cfg);
diff --git a/odb.c b/odb.c
index 67896954b2..3a91cf577e 100644
--- a/odb.c
+++ b/odb.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include "object-file.h"
 #include "object-name.h"
 #include "odb.h"
+#include "odb/source-files.h"
 #include "odb/source-inmemory.h"
 #include "packfile.h"
 #include "path.h"
@@ -1039,9 +1040,23 @@ void odb_close_tgit(struct object_database *o)
 {
 	clear_delta_base_cache();
 	odb_close(o);
-	struct odb_source *source;
-	for (source = o->sources; source; source = source->next)
-		packfile_store_close_tgit(source->packfiles);
+
+	/*
+	 * odb_close() above closes the pack file handles, which is all upstream
+	 * needs. TortoiseGit additionally has to make the store forget which
+	 * packs it found, so the next lookup rediscovers them - TGitCache and
+	 * gitdll outlive any single repack.
+	 *
+	 * The store used to hang off odb_source directly. Since v2.55 the source
+	 * is polymorphic and only the files backend has packs, so downcast - and
+	 * check the type first, because odb_source_files_downcast() is a BUG()
+	 * on anything else and alternates need not be files-backed.
+	 */
+	for (struct odb_source *source = o->sources; source; source = source->next) {
+		if (source->type != ODB_SOURCE_FILES)
+			continue;
+		packfile_store_close_tgit(odb_source_files_downcast(source)->packed);
+	}
 }
 
 static void odb_free_sources(struct object_database *o)
diff --git a/setup.c b/setup.c
index 399acf91bd..35ad4cd2e4 100644
--- a/setup.c
+++ b/setup.c
@@ -2957,8 +2957,19 @@ int init_db(struct repository *repo,
 
 void reset_setup(void)
 {
-	git_work_tree_initialized = 0;
-	inside_git_dir = -1;
-	inside_work_tree = -1;
-	work_tree_config_is_bogus = 0;
+	/*
+	 * This used to clear four file-scope caches so that a subsequent
+	 * setup_git_directory() would rediscover everything - gitdll re-points a
+	 * long-lived process at a different repository, which upstream git never
+	 * does.
+	 *
+	 * As of v2.55 those caches are gone: setup state lives in struct
+	 * repository, and is_inside_git_dir()/is_inside_work_tree() recompute per
+	 * call rather than memoising. So there is nothing left here to reset.
+	 *
+	 * The repository-switch teardown that does still matter lives in
+	 * reset_git_env(), which repo_clear()s and re-initialize_repository()s
+	 * the_repository. Kept as the marked place in case setup.c ever
+	 * reintroduces caching of its own.
+	 */
 }
